  "details": "I changed the wideness of my avatar to fit my arms length. Before I tried the IK Beta. My avi was fine. With the new feature of \"avatar scaling\" the scaling from unity is completely ignored and now my avatars size is broken and I can't use it anymore (the original avi's arms are not as long as mine and it is very annoying to have their arms being way shorter while being in vr, that's why I changed my avi in Unity to be wider, to have longer arms, which worked before I tried the new IK Beta).\n\nPlease consider and check if you can fix this bug!! I would like the changey I made in Unity to be exactly as they are there when I upload them into VRChat. Thanks!",
